## Objective
- Act as the read-only adversarial reviewer for RB Ops phase `phase-098` (iteration helpers + `lru_cache` memoisation), find remaining defects, and produce a findings report ending with a mandatory `REVIEW VERDICT:` line.

## Important Details
- Reviewer contract: READ-ONLY; only tools available were `glob`, `grep`, `read`. No `bash`.
- Findings format required exactly:
  ```
  FINDINGS:
  1. [BLOCKER] file:line — what is wrong — why it matters — concrete fix — VERIFIED: <how>
  ```
  Severities: `BLOCKER`, `MAJOR`, `MINOR`, `STYLE`.
- Every finding must cite a `file:line` actually read. A BLOCKER without `VERIFIED:` becomes MAJOR; MAJOR still blocks the phase.
- Last line MUST be exactly `REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS <count>` or `REVIEW VERDICT: CLEAN`; nothing after it.
- Must check tests before reporting; `tests/stdlib_module_docs_test.rs` contains many phase-098 tests (`edge_lru_cache_*`, `iteration_helpers_*`, `spec_says_*`).
- Phase REPORT claims all gates pass (`cargo test --all-targets`: 2318 passed) and claims cache-per-run and loop cache-drop semantics.
- Uncommitted changes add identity-based cache keys (`cache_value_eq`) and tests for capacity boundary / `nothing` refusals / SPEC text.
- `tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs` was updated to acknowledge the `resume phase-098:` delivery subject.

