FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] src/bytecode/vm.rs:3191-3199 — a cache hit while a `map` is pending calls `advance_map`, which calls `call_function` for the next element (3140-3155); N consecutive hits therefore recurse N Rust frames. A `map` over repeated values through a decorated function misses once, then hits for every remaining element, so a large list overflows the host stack before any `Error::Limit`; hits push no VM frame and skip the depth guard (3182-3185). The tree-walker's `apply_map` is a loop (src/interpreter.rs:2760-2769), and the VM's own comment says the map design exists to avoid host-stack overflow (3093-3104), so the engines disagree and the compiled one aborts. — Fix: make the hit path iterative: have `start_map`/`advance_map` check the cache and loop over consecutive hits, or return a hit sentinel from `call_function` so the map driver loops instead of recursing; add a test that maps a large list of one repeated value. VERIFIED: static trace 3196 -> 3154 -> 3191; the only map+cache test uses `[1, 1, 1]` (tests/stdlib_module_docs_test.rs:1709-1720), so depth is never exercised.

2. [MAJOR] src/bytecode/vm.rs:2910 — the hidden declaration resolves the just-stored function by name via `get_var`, which searches locals before globals (1409-1415); a file module runs in a `globals_only` frame (3975-3978) whose `DEF_FUNCTION`/`STORE` bind only globals (3314-3318, 2316-2321), so a same-named local or parameter in the importer shadows the module's function. The cache is then attached to the importer's function (overwriting any cache it had) while the module's function stays uncached; if the local is not a function, the import fails with `lru_cache declaration 'f' is not a function`. The tree-walker registers by value at declaration (src/interpreter.rs:2264-2273), so the engines disagree. — Fix: in the LRU branch, read `self.globals` when `self.frames[frame].globals_only`, or pass the function value directly instead of re-resolving its name; add a module test whose decorated function name also exists in the importer. VERIFIED: static trace of the module frame and both binding paths; grep of tests shows no `lru_cache` module test.

3. [MAJOR] src/interpreter.rs:2253-2263 — the replacement lookup only checks `self.locals.last()`, but `run_iteration_body` pushes a fresh scope per turn (1064-1065) and truncates it (1078); inside a loop the last scope is empty at declaration time, so the previous turn's cache is never removed from the VM-level `self.caches` (471). The comment at 2247-2249 claims a loop declaration "cannot grow an unreachable cache per turn", which is false for the tree-walker; the bytecode drops it because a loop body reuses its frame scope (src/bytecode/vm.rs:3292-3305). With MAX_ITERATIONS at 1e6 this retains up to a million `LruCache`s. — Fix: make the cache part of the `FunctionValue` so it dies with the value, or track caches per scope and drop ids declared in the truncated scope (preserving escaped closures), and add a loop test; otherwise remove the claim. VERIFIED: static trace of 1065 -> 2253 -> 2261 and 1078; grep shows no loop+`lru_cache` test.

4. [MINOR] SURVEY.md:9-10 — the `BUILTIN_NAMES` anchors are stale: the declaration is at src/stdlib.rs:1190 and the closing `"input"` is at 1282, not 1200/1292; the same wrong anchors appear at SURVEY.md:196 and SURVEY.md:219. — Fix: update all three citations to 1190/1282. VERIFIED: read src/stdlib.rs:1190 and 1282.

5. [STYLE] src/interpreter.rs:3021-3022 — the comment says "The lookup is by declaration name", but the lookup uses `function.id` (3023-3026) and the phase deliberately keys by identity. — Fix: say the lookup is by function identity so two same-named declarations never share a cache. VERIFIED: read the comment and the adjacent lookup.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 5
